<article class="env-definition" id="06QC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06QC">Definition <span data-tag="06QC">101.28.1</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. We say $\mathcal{X}$ is a <em>gerbe over</em> $\mathcal{Y}$ if $\mathcal{X}$ is a gerbe over $\mathcal{Y}$ as stacks in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, see Stacks, Definition <a href="/tag/06P2" data-tag="06P2">8.11.4</a>. We say an algebraic stack $\mathcal{X}$ is a <em>gerbe</em> if there exists a morphism $\mathcal{X} \to X$ where $X$ is an algebraic space which turns $\mathcal{X}$ into a gerbe over $X$. </p>
</article>